# Part U: the tool's functions on small inputs

## U1 (L39): code lines, round 6 against round 7
K1 a triple-quoted argument:
  1: round 6 code | round 7 code | @triton.jit
  2: round 6 code | round 7 code | def k(c, x_ptr):
  3: round 6 code | round 7 code |     x = tl.load(x_ptr)
  4: round 6 ---- | round 7 code |     tl.device_print("""x""", tl.atomic_add(c, 1))
  5: round 6 code | round 7 code |     tl.store(x_ptr, x)
K2 triple quotes in two comments:
  1: round 6 code | round 7 code | @triton.jit
