## U2 (L38): the manifest check
the real manifest: no problem
the namespace of lr-6a's injection: ['lean.namespace must be a dotted name of ASCII letters, digits, `_` and `\'` (found \'Nat), True := fun _ => trivial\\n#eval IO.println "x"\\n#exit\\n--\')']
a module with a line break: ["lean.module must be a dotted name of ASCII letters, digits, `_` and `'` (found 'VecAdd\\n#exit')"]
a namespace with a space: ["lean.namespace must be a dotted name of ASCII letters, digits, `_` and `'` (found 'Kernels.Vec Add')"]
a source file outside the kernel folder: ["source.file must be a path inside the kernel folder (found '<three folders up>/README.md')"]

## U3 (L40): the library hygiene's view of Lean code (comments removed, literals kept)
a command after a string holding --: ['meta code']
